# Clean public repos

When committing, pushing, or writing README/LICENSE/docs for GitHub/GitLab (this and future apps):

- No keystore files, passwords, tokens, PATs, `keystore.properties`, `BACKUP-THIS.txt`, private keys, fingerprints published as identity docs
- No absolute or home paths (`/Users/...`, `~/Projects/...`, machine-specific `JAVA_HOME`, SDK paths)
- No Author-ID / anti-theft manifesto / DMCA essays that look AI-written
- README: short human text — what it is, how to build, where version lives
- LICENSE: short proprietary blurb is enough
- Keep signing material local and gitignored (`keystore/`, `*.jks`, `keystore.properties`)
- Do not put personal brand IDs, fingerprints, or backup instructions in the public tree unless the user explicitly asks

